# Crypto Screener Columns loop — self-paced, read roadmap and execute first unchecked task
# Run: claude "/loop $(cat CRYPTO_LOOP.sh | tail -1)"
# Or paste the prompt line below into claude with /loop

Read docs/CRYPTO_SCREENER_ROADMAP.md and follow its hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task. Hard rules recap: NO new serverless files under apps/market-ui/api (Hobby 12-fn cap; new server data goes into api/crypto/markets.ts or klines.ts via ?view= query params; never a dynamic [fn].ts under /api/crypto/ — the vercel.json Fly rewrite shadows dynamic routes); keyless APIs only (CoinGecko free, Binance public spot+fapi, coinlore/OKX fallbacks preserved) and curl-verify an endpoint returns real data BEFORE coding against it; no new npm deps (hand-roll RSI/EMA/MACD/BB/ATR math); payload changes additive only — existing MarketData fields and the coingecko→coinlore→okx fallback chain must keep working; UI uses project design tokens and matches the existing popover style in Markets.tsx. Verify: UI/server tasks need market-ui typecheck 0 errors + vercel --prod + curl of the prod endpoint with REAL numbers pasted into the Progress log. Flip the task to [x], append one Progress-log line with real numbers, commit on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). PERSISTENCE: never end the loop because of a usage/rate limit, 429, or overloaded error — on any such error stop consuming tokens, ScheduleWakeup at 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log are recovery state; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations); chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining, or a task blocked on something only the user can provide — then say exactly what's needed and still ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes if supplied.
